@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-individual`
IMPORT `ito-s2-charge-and-s2a`
IMPORT `ito-il29-test-people`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-29 tests: s 2 (the territorial charge, with both statuses of s 1) and s 2A (winnings).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew text BEFORE the code was run.
-- ===========================================================================

`D` MEANS `the default readings of row IL-29`

GIVEN produced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An item of income, for the charge of section 2`
`an item produced in Israel:` produced MEANS `An item of income, for the charge of section 2` WITH `produced or accrued in Israel` IS produced, `amount` IS 100

§ `Section 2: the territorial charge`

-- An Israeli resident (and not a foreign resident): income produced or accrued in Israel or outside it.
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` TRUE)
-- A foreign resident (not an Israeli resident): income produced or accrued in Israel only.
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` TRUE)
-- Both (the second limb of "foreign resident" met by one who is also an Israeli resident, fork BS): income produced in Israel is
-- charged on either reading, so the default answers; income produced abroad is charged on one reading and not the other: declined.
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` FALSE) BECAUSE "the person is both an Israeli resident and a foreign resident (the second limb of the definition of foreign resident), and the text does not say which status the charge of s 2 reads: worldwide income, or income produced or accrued in Israel only"
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` (`the defaults, except both statuses read` `the foreign resident status prevails`) `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` (`the defaults, except both statuses read` `the Israeli resident status prevails`) `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` FALSE)
-- Neither: the two definitions leave no such person.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2 — the item is within the charge, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`an item produced in Israel:` TRUE) BECAUSE "the person is neither an Israeli resident nor a foreign resident, which the definitions do not allow"

§ `Section 2A: winnings from gambling, lotteries and prize-bearing activity`

GIVEN resident IS A BOOLEAN
      produced IS A BOOLEAN
      other    IS A BOOLEAN
      personal IS A BOOLEAN
      minister IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Winnings under section 2A`
`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` resident `, produced in Israel:` produced `, other source:` other `, personal prize:` personal `, determined by the Minister:` minister MEANS
    `Winnings under section 2A` WITH
        `the winner is an Israeli resident` IS resident
        `produced or accrued in Israel` IS produced
        `income from another source under the Ordinance` IS other
        `a prize given in a personal setting` IS personal
        `a lottery or prize determined by the Minister of Finance with the approval of the Finance Committee` IS minister
        `amount` IS 1000

-- (a): a resident's winnings, wherever produced; a foreign resident's, if produced in Israel.
#ASSERT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` TRUE `, produced in Israel:` FALSE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` FALSE `, produced in Israel:` FALSE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` FALSE `, produced in Israel:` TRUE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE)
-- (b)(1), (2), (3): each takes the winnings outside paragraph (a).
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` TRUE `, produced in Israel:` TRUE `, other source:` TRUE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` TRUE `, produced in Israel:` TRUE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` TRUE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` FALSE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` TRUE `, produced in Israel:` TRUE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` TRUE)
-- Both statuses (fork BS) apply to winnings as to income: abroad is declined, in Israel answers.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` TRUE `, produced in Israel:` FALSE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE) BECAUSE "the person is both an Israeli resident and a foreign resident (the second limb of the definition of foreign resident), and the text does not say which status the charge of s 2 reads: worldwide income, or income produced or accrued in Israel only"
#ASSERT `s 2A — the winnings are taken into account and deemed income by section 2A, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `and a foreign resident:` TRUE `, under` `D` `:` (`winnings of a winner who is a resident:` TRUE `, produced in Israel:` TRUE `, other source:` FALSE `, personal prize:` FALSE `, determined by the Minister:` FALSE)
-- Except for the set-off of losses.
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A deems the winnings income for the purpose of the set-off of losses`
